WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:02.860
Hey guys, it's Jan here.

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:06.970
If you've seen my review of Star Wars: The
Force Awakens, you'll know I really enjoyed

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:07.970
the movie.

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:11.900
And, of course, there's a wealth of call-backs
and easter eggs throughout the film, so I've

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:16.100
put together as many of those eggs and references
as I could find in this video.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:20.789
I know you'll have spotted other cool ones
too, so do share them in the comments below!

00:00:20.789 --> 00:00:24.910
Just a quick reminder there will be spoilers
ahead, so if you're not ready for that, check

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.759
out my non-spoiler review of the movie here!

00:00:27.759 --> 00:00:32.820
The franchise's description of the Millennium
Falcon as junk continues in The Force Awakens,

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:35.020
when Rey twice refers to it as garbage.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:39.340
Of course, Luke called it a "piece of junk"
in A New Hope, Lando said "she's the fastest

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:43.500
hunk of junk in the galaxy" in The Empire
Strikes Back, and Han Solo himself called

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.500
it a "piece of junk" in Return of the Jedi.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:49.320
But when Rey says to Han about the Falcon,
"It's the ship that made the Kessel Run in

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:53.821
fourteen parsecs" and he corrects her, it's
a nice nod to when Han boasted to Obi Wan

00:00:53.821 --> 00:00:58.059
and Luke that the Millennium Falcon made the
Kessel Run in less than 12 parsecs.

00:00:58.059 --> 00:01:01.940
The Falcon's circular sensor dish has been
replaced with a rectangular one for The Force

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:06.170
Awakens as the original was lost when Lando
flew the ship in Return of the Jedi.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:09.590
And there's a nice little call-back with a
twist to that incident when Rey clips the

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:13.140
underneath of the Falcon as it flies off Jakku
into space.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:17.580
As for motivators, well they're a recurring
problem in the world of Star Wars, for example,

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:21.979
when Rey examines the fault on the Millennium
Falcon she exclaims "it's the motivator";

00:01:21.979 --> 00:01:26.450
in The Empire Strikes Back, C-3PO says he
noticed the hyperdrive motivator was damaged;

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:30.420
and in A New Hope, Luke says "This R2 unit
has a bad motivator".

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:33.909
And the classic Star Wars line, 'I got a bad
feeling about this', which has appeared in

00:01:33.909 --> 00:01:39.130
all the previous Star Wars movies, is delivered
by Han Solo when he hears a rathtar roar after

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:41.540
Rey accidentally releases the beasts.

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:45.689
When the Rathtar's eye suddenly appears at
the window looking at Han, Finn and Rey, it

00:01:45.689 --> 00:01:49.740
feels like a little nod to Jurassic Park,
which seems apt given that Jurassic World

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.850
director Colin Trevorrow is directing Star
Wars Episode 9.

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:56.810
Later, when they're trying to escape, Finn
picks up the Jedi Remote Training Ball we

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:59.079
see Luke Skywalker training with in A New
Hope.

00:01:59.079 --> 00:02:04.009
And after they've escaped, Finn accidentally
turns on the holochess table from A New Hope.

00:02:04.009 --> 00:02:10.230
And the number in Finn's Stormtrooper designation
FN-2187 is a reference to Cell 2187 where

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.630
Leia was held captive.

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:16.150
Oh, and by the way, when Finn tells Han that
his job as a Stormtrooper was sanitation,

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:20.370
it's an easter egg to super-fan Kevin Smith's
movie Clerks, where one of the characters

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:24.110
wonders if the 'average Stormtrooper knows
how to install a toilet main'.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:28.560
Speaking of easter eggs to other movies, there's
a great visual of TIE fighters silhouetted

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:32.920
against the sun which is reminiscent of Francis
Ford Coppolla's Apocalypse Now.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:36.250
And when Han Solo says that he used to think
the Force and the Jedi were 'mumbo jumbo',

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:40.530
it's is a funny little easter egg as that
was a phrase actor Alec Guinness, who played

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:44.310
Jedi Obi Wan Kenobi, used to describe the
Star Wars script.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:48.550
After the opening crawl, there's an instant
call-back to Star Wars: A New Hope, with the

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:52.610
camera panning down to a similar shot of two
moons or planets with the smaller one to the

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:54.340
upper right of the larger one.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:58.360
And the way the huge Star Destroyer completely
eclipsed the moons at the start of The Force

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:02.450
Awakens is an interesting nod to the script
for A New Hope which says "The awesome yellow

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.710
planet of Tatooine emerges from a total eclipse."

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:11.280
Back on Jakku, Poe Dameron hiding the map
to Luke Skywalker's location inside BB-8 after

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:15.870
he's tracked down by The First Order recalls
how Leia hid the schematics for the Death

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:19.450
Star in R2-D2 after her ship was captured
by The Empire.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:22.871
And after BB-8 flees the village razed by
the First Order, a pair of glowing eyes pop

00:03:22.871 --> 00:03:24.310
up out of a sand dune.

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:28.780
The way the eyes pop up are a call back to
when R2-D2's periscope emerged from the sand

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:31.250
dunes after he fell off Jabba The Hutt's sail
barge.

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:35.830
And they also look kind of like Hem Dazon
from the Mos Eisley cantina scene in A New

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:36.830
Hope.

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:41.940
They may even be a be a little nod to director
JJ Abrams' production company Bad Robot.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:47.520
When BB-8 is caught by Teedo, it's a call-back
to A New Hope when R2-D2 is captured by Jawas.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:52.040
BB-8's response to Rey that his mission is
classified feels a lot like when Luke asked

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:57.700
R2-D2 to play back Leia's entire message and
R2-D2 says it's a private message for Obi-Wan

00:03:57.700 --> 00:03:58.700
Kenobi.

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:03.150
When Rey gives BB-8 directions, she advises
him to stay off Kelvin Ridge.

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:07.440
The name Kelvin is a regular easter egg in
JJ Abrams' productions and is an homage to

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:13.930
his grandfather Harry Kelvin.

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:24.390
BB-8 actually wants to go with Rey, and although
she refuses, BB-8 eventually gets his own

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:25.390
way.

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:29.920
Which is a nice nod to when R2-D2 wants to
go with Luke and C-3PO in A New Hope, but

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:32.530
is initially stopped by one of the Jawa traders.

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:38.080
Rey's home on Jakku is in the wreck of an
AT-AT walker and inside is a straw doll which

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:41.540
looks like it's wearing an X-Wing pilot's
uniform.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:46.780
Outside when Rey puts on a beaten-up helmet,
on the side you can make out 3 Aurebesh letters

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:50.660
which translate to R-A-EH, or Rey.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:54.441
And the glasses she wears while scavenging
look like they're made with lenses from a

00:04:54.441 --> 00:04:55.750
Stormtrooper helmet.

00:04:55.750 --> 00:05:01.230
Later when Rey and BB-8 are interrogating
Finn about why he has Poe's jacket, BB-8 gives

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:06.470
Finn a quick zap, like how R2-D2 zaps C-3PO
while he's repairing him at the end of The

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:07.760
Empire Strikes Back.

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:11.510
And the design of the gate at the junk-yard
on Jakku was taken from unused concept art

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:15.230
by Ralph McQuarrie for Jabba The Hutt's palace
in the original trilogy.

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:20.820
In 2013, on the Conan O'Brien show, JJ Abrams
agreed to include one of Conan's favourite

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.280
phrases "Jub Jub" into The Force Awakens.

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:27.600
It sounds like you can hear "jub jub" said
by one of the aliens on Jakku when Finn and

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:29.830
Rey are being chased by the Stormtroopers.

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:34.420
The scene at Maz Kanata's place with an assortment
of crazy-looking aliens being entertained

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:39.400
by a reggae-style band was definitely reminiscent
of the Mos Eisley cantina scene in A New Hope.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:43.820
And hanging outside her bar there are a stack
of banners, many of which appear as Podracer

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.550
flags in The Phantom Menace.

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:50.890
The most noticeable one perhaps is the Mandalorian
banner seen on fan-favourite Boba Fett's armour.

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:55.850
The crying Rey hears in Maz's basement and
the vision she experiences with Kylo Ren after

00:05:55.850 --> 00:06:00.560
finding Luke's lost lightsaber is reminiscent
of The Empire Strikes Back scene where Luke

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:05.170
descends into a cave full of strange noises
and has a vision where he fights Darth Vader.

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:08.100
And Darth Vader's presence is felt in many
of Kylo Ren's scenes.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:13.130
For example, when Kylo goes before Supreme
Leader Snoke, Snoke says to him "There has

00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:14.130
been an awakening.

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:18.800
Have you felt it?", an echo of the Emperor's
words in The Empire Strikes Back: "There is

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:23.450
a great disturbance in the Force" and Darth
Vader's response "I have felt it."

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:27.850
And Kylo's words to Snoke that "By the grace
of your training, I will not be seduced",

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:32.530
the implication being "to the light side",
are a call-back with a twist to Obi-Wan's

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:37.290
explanation to Luke in A New Hope and again
in Return of the Jedi that his father Anakin

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:40.470
Skywalker "was seduced by the dark side of
the Force".

00:06:40.470 --> 00:06:44.880
And Snoke's words to Kylo that "The droid
we seek is aboard the Millennium Falcon" is

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:49.770
an echo of Obi Wan's words "These aren't the
droids you're looking for" in A New Hope.

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:54.830
The deformed mask Kylo talks to is Darth Vader's
mask from the funeral pyre Luke built for

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:57.230
his father on Endor at the end of Return of
the Jedi.

00:06:57.230 --> 00:07:02.270
When Han Solo tells Leia, 'there's too much
Vader in him' about Kylo, it's a call-back

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:07.800
to A New Hope when Luke's Aunt says to Owen
that Luke "has too much of his father in him".

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:12.310
Leia's reply to Han that "there's still light
in him" echoes Luke's words about Darth Vader

00:07:12.310 --> 00:07:14.000
that "there's still good in him."

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:18.470
And the connection between Darth Vader and
Kylo Ren is further emphasised when Han tells

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:24.290
Finn and Rey that Luke was training a new
Jedi generation and one boy, an apprentice,

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:28.530
turned against him and destroyed it all, which
echoes what happened when Anakin turned against

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:30.730
the Jedi Order in Revenge of the Sith.

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:36.950
Kylo Ren's real name, Ben Solo, might be a
nod to Obi Wan Kenobi's alias of "Ben Kenobi"

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:40.610
that Obi Wan used after exiling himself to
Tatooine.

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:45.010
By the way the character of Ben Solo seems
to also draw inspiration from the character

00:07:45.010 --> 00:07:50.070
of Jacen Solo who is Han and Leia's son in
The Legacy of the Force book series and who,

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:53.220
like Kylo, turned to the dark side to become
Darth Caedus.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:58.090
We didn't get any exact Vader-esque Force
Chokes, but Kylo did something similar when

00:07:58.090 --> 00:08:01.990
he pulled an officer towards him through the
air and started choking him directly with

00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:03.330
his gloved hand.

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:08.139
And on board the Star Destroyer, a mouse-droid
scoots by while Poe Dameron's being marched

00:08:08.139 --> 00:08:12.150
along as a prisoner, which is a nice call-back
to when Chewbacca yells at a mouse-droid in

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:16.120
A New Hope while he's being escorted as a
prisoner by Han and Luke dressed as stormtroopers.

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:21.350
There are some great moments with C-3PO such
as when he pops up suddenly just after Han

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:26.210
and Leia reunite for the first time, which
is a sweet call-back to when C-3PO interrupts

00:08:26.210 --> 00:08:28.910
Han and Leia's kiss in The Empire Strikes
Back.

00:08:28.910 --> 00:08:34.960
And After R2-D2 reactivates and starts talking
to C-3PO, the protocol droid exclaims "how

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:36.200
dare you call me that!"

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:41.240
a fun call-back to the numerous insults they've
traded and arguments they've had all over

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:42.240
the series.

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:45.730
C-3PO gets to deliver one of his favourite
phrases "we're doomed!"

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:50.130
when Starkiller Base starts to prepare its
weapon to fire on the Resistance base.

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:55.230
And when C-3PO exclaims "Thank the maker"
when the shields come down on Starkiller Base,

00:08:55.230 --> 00:09:00.020
it's a nice call-back to the same phrase in
A New Hope when C-3PO takes an oil bath.

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:04.810
The name Starkiller is a reference to "Luke
Starkiller", which was the name for Luke Skywalker

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:07.420
in early drafts of the first Star Wars movie.

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:11.170
And on Starkiller Base, there's a great line
when Han Solo asks what they should do with

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:15.770
the captured Captain Phasma, and he wonders
if there's a garbage chute or trash compactor.

00:09:15.770 --> 00:09:20.920
It's a lovely reference to the scene in a
New Hope where Han, Leia, Luke and Chewbacca

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:24.070
escape down a chute only to end up in a Garbage
Compactor.

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:29.400
By the way, Captain Phasma's name was inspired
by the 1979 horror film, Phantasm, in which

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:32.000
the villain attacks his victims with a silver
sphere.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:37.240
Hangar 718 where the First Order searches
for the escaped Rey could be a nod to the

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:43.040
AT-AT walker Unit 718-A which appears in the
Star Wars short story Easy Credits.

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:47.339
And the charges Han and Chewie set up to disable
the shield in Starkiller Base are a call-back

00:09:47.339 --> 00:09:51.920
to when they both used explosive charges to
destroy the shield generator on Endor in Return

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:52.920
of the Jedi.

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:56.980
And the shiny round design of the explosives
they use is reminiscent of the silver sphere

00:09:56.980 --> 00:10:02.080
in the 70s movie Phantasm, which JJ Abrams'
company Bad Robot is restoring.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:06.850
The X-Wing attack on Starkiller which first
begins along a trench and then dives into

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:11.370
the core of the superweapon is a nod to the
way the Rebel fighters destroyed the Death

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:14.020
Stars in both A New Hope and Return of the
Jedi.

00:10:14.020 --> 00:10:17.970
The name of X-Wing fighter "Ello Asty", who
dies during the attack, is a reference to

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:20.339
the Beastie Boys album "Hello Nasty".

00:10:20.339 --> 00:10:24.420
In Rey and Kylo's final face-off when she
uses the Force to pull the lightsaber that's

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:28.690
wedged in the snow, it's a call-back to how
Luke summons the lightsaber that's stuck in

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:31.510
the snow while he's trapped in the Wampa's
cave on Hoth.

00:10:31.510 --> 00:10:36.330
And Kylo's words "You need a teacher, I can
show you the ways of the Force" to Rey during

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:40.720
the duel echoes The Empire Strikes Back when
Vader tells Luke to join him and he will complete

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:41.890
Luke's training.

00:10:41.890 --> 00:10:46.290
And when Rey injures Kylo on the shoulder,
it's a call-back to Luke wounding Darth Vader

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:49.660
in their lightsaber battle at the end of The
Empire Strikes Back.

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:53.640
And there's some Star Wars limb loss when
the Rathtar which is dragging Finn off loses

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:57.370
2 of its tentacles when Rey closes one of
the blast doors on the creature.

00:10:57.370 --> 00:11:02.770
Later in the final battle between Rey and
Kylo Ren it almost looks like she slices his

00:11:02.770 --> 00:11:07.860
arm or hand off but if you look closely when
Kylo sits up you can see his arm and hand

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:09.940
still attached and moving.

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:14.140
And, of course, C-3PO refers to the fact that
he previously lost his arm and had it replaced

00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:15.140
with a red one.

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:19.880
Also, in the novelisation of The Force Awakens
by Alan Dean Foster there's a scene where

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:23.890
Unkar Plutt has tracked down Rey to Maz Kanata's
cantina.

00:11:23.890 --> 00:11:28.680
In the ensuing confrontation Chewbacca rips
off one of Unkar Plutt's arm.

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:33.630
JJ Abrams has confirmed there's around a dozen
deleted scenes so I wonder if that will be

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:34.630
among them?

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:39.279
Another Star Wars regular, the scum insult
returns when Rey tries to mind-trick the stormtrooper

00:11:39.279 --> 00:11:43.600
guarding her and he responds, "I'll tighten
those restraints, scavenger scum".

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:46.040
The "scum" insult's appeared in most of the
movies, for example, "Freeze!

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:49.130
You rebel scum" in Return of the Jedi.

00:11:49.130 --> 00:11:54.080
By the way, Bond himself, Daniel Craig actually
cameoed as the Stormtrooper who's mind-tricked

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:55.080
by Rey.

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:57.370
And there's tons of other cameos in the movie.

00:11:57.370 --> 00:12:01.990
Carrie Fisher's daughter Billie Lourd makes
an appearance as Lieutenant Connix, and her

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:05.870
character also sports some Princess Leia-esque
buns in her hair.

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:10.100
Thomas Brodie-Sangster, aka Jojen Reed in
Game of Thrones or Newt from The Maze Runner

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:14.660
movies, cameos as a First Order officer who
reports an unsanctioned departure from Bay

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:17.339
2 as Finn and Poe Dameron try to escape.

00:12:17.339 --> 00:12:21.680
Michael Giacchino, who composed the music
for many of JJ Abram's productions, cameos

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:24.520
as Stormtrooper FN-3181.

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:30.640
And his Stormtrooper number 3181 could be
rearranged as 1138, a hidden nod to George

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:35.100
Lucas' 1971 film THX 1138.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:39.370
Radiohead producer Nigel Godrich is also credited
as Stormtrooper FN-9330.

00:12:39.370 --> 00:12:43.330
Simon Pegg plays junk-yard trader Unkar Plutt.

00:12:43.330 --> 00:12:47.839
While Warwick Davis, who played Wicket the
Ewok in Return of the Jedi, plays the role

00:12:47.839 --> 00:12:50.149
of Wollivan, and appears in Maz Kanata's bar.

00:12:50.149 --> 00:12:55.149
And comedian Judah Friedlander, who plays
Frank in 30 Rock, is another of the bar patrons.

00:12:55.149 --> 00:13:00.350
Miltos Yerolemou, aka Syrio Forel in Game
of Thrones, is another bar patron who you

00:13:00.350 --> 00:13:04.950
can see just to the right of Han Solo outside
the bar as they all look up at the sky at

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:07.780
the destruction caused by the Starkiller superweapon.

00:13:07.780 --> 00:13:14.460
JJ Abrams' assistant Morgan Dameron is humorously
credited in the movie as Commodore Meta, with

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:18.880
Meta probably being a little joke about the
fact that Poe Dameron's surname was inspired

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:19.880
by her.

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:20.880
Abrams also cast his father Gerry Abrams as
Captain Cypress.

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:21.880
Gerry Abrams is a TV producer and founder
of the production company Cypress Point Productions.

00:13:21.880 --> 00:13:24.589
JJ Abrams also cast his lucky charm regular
and former Lost actor Greg Grunberg as X-Wing

00:13:24.589 --> 00:13:26.640
pilot Snap Wexley.

00:13:26.640 --> 00:13:31.070
Lost actor Ken Leung also appears in The Force
Awakens as Resistance Admiral Statura.

00:13:31.070 --> 00:13:36.240
And it wouldn't be a JJ Abrams' film without
at least one of his signature lens flares.

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:41.330
More cameos include Game of Thrones Sand Snake,
actor Jessica Henwick who plays an X-wing

00:13:41.330 --> 00:13:42.330
fighter.

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:46.440
Mark Stanley, aka Grenn from Game of Thrones,
appears briefly in Rey's vision as one of

00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:47.490
the Knights of Ren.

00:13:47.490 --> 00:13:52.150
And The Raid's Iko Uwais and Yayan Ruhian
appear as members of the Kanjiclub Gang who

00:13:52.150 --> 00:13:54.080
are after Han Solo who owes them money.

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:58.250
Admiral Ackbar and Nien Nunb also return from
the original trilogy with cameos.

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:02.519
And comedians Bill Hader and Ben Schwartz
both contributed to the voice of BB-8.

00:14:02.519 --> 00:14:07.410
The name of Resistance commander Colonel Kaplan
is a nod to Michael Kaplan, the movie's costume

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:08.410
designer.

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:12.450
And the final words spoken in the movie are
"May The Force Be With You", which Leia says

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:14.870
to Rey before she leaves to find Luke.

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:19.970
It's also the final phrase in The Empire Strikes
Back and is said by Luke to Lando and Chewbacca

00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:22.660
who are leaving to rescue Han Solo from Jabba
The Hutt.

